{"parentUuid":"9bf31f6d-5fe9-4631-8165-a9d8eac98606","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/suyashkumar/cli","sessionId":"1efe396a-fe7c-42ab-b835-a4ad514b68b9","version":"2.1.39","gitBranch":"luffysk/test","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017fLiV7KYPzbwpW22qm8xYa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Entire CLI Repository\n\nThis is the **CLI tool for Entire**, built in Go. Here's a high-level overview:\n\n## What It Does\n\nThe CLI manages **session checkpoints** for coding agents (like Claude Code). It tracks what an AI agent does during a session — saving snapshots of code changes, session transcripts, and metadata — so users can **rewind** to previous points if needed.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Strategies\nThe central abstraction is the **Strategy pattern** for how session data is stored:\n\n| Strategy | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| **manual-commit** (default) | Never touches your branch. Stores checkpoints on hidden shadow branches (`entire/<hash>-<hash>`). You commit manually when ready. |\n| **auto-commit** | Creates real commits on your branch with clean history, plus metadata on an orphan branch. |\n\nBoth strategies store session metadata (transcripts, prompts, context) on an orphan branch called `entire/checkpoints/v1`.\n\n### Checkpoints & Rewind\n- Each checkpoint captures a snapshot of code changes + session metadata\n- Users can list checkpoints (`GetRewindPoints`) and restore to any previous one (`Rewind`)\n- A 12-hex-char **checkpoint ID** links user commits to their metadata via a `Entire-Checkpoint` git trailer\n\n### Session Lifecycle\nSessions go through phases managed by a state machine: `ACTIVE` → `IDLE` → `ENDED`, triggered by events like `TurnStart`, `TurnEnd`, `GitCommit`.\n\n## Key Directory Structure\n\n- **`cmd/entire/`** — Main entry point\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/commands/`** — Command implementations (cobra commands)\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`** — Strategy implementations (manual-commit, auto-commit)\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/`** — Checkpoint storage (temporary on shadow branches, committed on metadata branch)\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/session/`** — Session state management and phase state machine\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`** — Integration tests\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- **Go 1.25.x** with cobra (CLI framework) and huh (interactive TUI forms)\n- **go-git** for most git operations (with CLI fallback for `checkout`/`reset --hard` due to a go-git bug that deletes `.gitignore`d directories)\n- **golangci-lint** for linting, **mise** as the task runner\n\n## Git Hook Integration\n\nThe CLI installs git hooks (`prepare-commit-msg`, `post-commit`, `pre-push`) to:\n- Add checkpoint trailers to commits\n- Trigger condensation (copying session data to the permanent metadata branch)\n- Optionally push the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch alongside user pushes\n\nIn short: it's a **version-control layer on top of git** specifically designed to track and manage AI coding sessions, giving users the ability to inspect what happened and roll back changes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27073,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":27073,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"}},"requestId":"req_011CY2HfJHa4HMbZDZri8v2t","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a72d50f-8633-4f62-8cbe-d7199acbae86","timestamp":"2026-02-11T12:33:36.821Z"}
